  "recipeCuisine": "France",
  "name": "Chicken chasseur",
  "text": "Chicken chasseur\n\nYield: Serves 4\n\nIngredients\n\nFor the chicken\n\n1.5 kg chicken (cut into 8 pieces},\n\nsalt and freshly ground black pepper,\n\n50 g plain flour\n\n2 tbsp olive oil\n\n110g butter\n\n175g button mushrooms\n\n150g shallots, thickly sliced\n\n40g caster sugar\n\n175ml white wine\n\n350ml chicken stock\n\n3 tbsp tomato purée\n\nsmall handful fresh tarragon, half left as sprigs, half finely chopped\n\n2 tomatoes, peeled, seeds removed, chopped\n\n2 tbsp fresh flatleaf parsley, finely chopped\n\nFor the mashed potatoes\n\n1 kg floury potatoes (such as King Edwards or Desiree), peeled,\n\ncut into chunks\n\n110 g butter\n\n110 ml oz full fat milk\n\nsalt and freshly ground black pepper\n\nPreparation method\n\n1. Season the chicken pieces with salt and freshly ground black pepper,\n\nthen dredge in the flour to coat.\n\n2. Heat a large, deep frying pan over a medium heat. Add the oil, and a\n\nthird of the butter and heat until the butter is foaming.\n\n3. Add the chicken pieces and fry skin-side down for 1-2 minutes until\n\ngolden-brown, then turn the chicken and fry on the other side for\n\nanother 1-2 minutes.\n\n4.Meanwhile, heat a separate frying pan over a medium heat and add\n\nanother third of the butter. When the butter is foaming add the button\n\nmushrooms and fry, stirring occasionally, until golden-brown all over.\n\n5. Add the mushrooms to the chicken pan.\n\n6. To the pan used to fry the mushrooms, add the remaining third of the\n\nbutter, the shallots and the caster sugar and fry for 2-3 minutes until\n\nthe shallots are golden-brown and caramelised.\n\n7. Add the wine and bring to the boil, scraping the base of the pan with\n\na wooden spoon to dislodge any brown bits.\n\n8. Pour the shallots and wine mixture over the chicken, then add the\n\nstock, tomato purée and whole tarragon sprigs. Bring to the boil, then\n\nreduce the heat to simmer for 45 minutes to one hour, or until the\n\nchicken is completely cooked through and the sauce has reduced\n\nslightly.\n\n9. Add the tomatoes, flatleaf parsley and the chopped tarragon and\n\nseason, to taste, with salt and freshly ground black pepper. Simmer\n\nfor a further two minutes.\n\n10.Meanwhile, for the mashed potatoes, place the potatoes into a pan\n\nof salted water and bring to the boil. Reduce the heat and simmer\n\nfor 12-15 minutes, or until the potatoes are tender.\n\n11. Drain the potatoes and return to the pan. Place over a low heat for\n\none minute to drive off any excess moisture.\n\n12.Mash the potatoes well, then add the butter and milk, beating well\n\nto form a smooth mash. Season, to taste, with salt and freshly\n\nground black pepper.\n\n13. To serve, place two pieces of chicken onto each plate. Drizzle the\n\nsauce over each and place a dollop of mashed potatoes alongside.",
  "recipeYield": "Serves 4",
